@talks work:garden
// TW1, the Talk a while work pools: Garden (plans/work-pools-plan.html, decided 2026-10-20). Cruz, O'Neill, Hart.
// Ids work.garden.<slug>; topic always "work". Never the blue sage (Brennan's arc, beat 2). Cruz is shy and on the
// lonely theme; O'Neill notgood: no doubt talk.

== first-light
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:hart-ravi
them: Hart does the first watering, start of the early team. Every day. Without fail.
them: I came in early once and it was like walking into rain. Proper rain. I nearly cried.   #warm
ask: What's the first thing you do, every morning?
listen: Does the garden like the early water?
  them: Plants like routine. Same time, same amount. Like the rest of us, really.
share: Check the board. Then breakfast.
  them: Good order. The garden's the other way round. Breakfast after.
cheer: Hit the snooze. Twice.
  them: The garden forgives you. The tomatoes are judging, though.   #funny

== gerald-nursery
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: The Gerald tray needs turning every morning, or they all lean the same way.
them: Seventeen in there right now. Each one's somebody's, soon.   #warm
ask: Is there a job you do that's really for someone you haven't met yet?
listen: Who gets the next one?
  them: Whoever needs one. You can always tell. They stand very still by the tray.   #warm
share: Fixing things for the next shift.
  them: Same thing. Somebody you'll never meet, glad it works. Lovely.   #warm
cheer: Leaving the tape in the second drawer.
  them: A gift to the future. Works will thank you. Silently.   #funny

== herbs-galley
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: Every evening I pick the galley's herbs. Brennan wants them fresh. Very fresh.
them: I take them up with ten minutes to spare. If I'm late, I hear about it. Kindly. Loudly.   #funny
ask: Who's the person you'd never want to keep waiting?
listen: What does Brennan say if you're late?
  them: "Lovely. Thank you so very much." Very polite. Terrifying. Never late again.   #funny
share: Calder. Never.
  them: Wise. Calder doesn't say anything. That's worse.   #funny
cheer: My dinner. It waits for no one.
  them: Correct. Dinner waits for nobody. Not even gardeners.   #funny

== garden-why
when: tier>=colleague
them: I chose the garden because everything in it is trying. Every leaf, every root. All trying.
them: It's hard to have a bad day surrounded by things trying that hard.   #warm
ask: Is there a place aboard that makes your bad days lighter?
listen: Do plants ever give up?
  them: Some do. Then we try something else. You learn a lot from the ones that don't make it.
share: Here, actually. The garden.
  them: Then come more often. Sit by the big tree. Nobody minds.   #warm
cheer: The mess. Specifically the pudding.
  them: Pudding's a garden thing too, if you think about it. Very loosely.   #funny

== garden-means
when: tier>=friend !who:cruz-tove
them: Know what the garden means to me? A whole ship breathing air we helped clean.
them: And eating herbs we grew. And smelling rain in a ship. That's a lot from a tray of soil.   #warm
ask: What's the small thing you do that matters more than it looks?
listen: Do people know how much the garden does?
  them: No. And that's fine. They come in and breathe. We count that as applause.   #warm
share: Keeping the air clean. Same as you.
  them: Ha. Then we're partners, aren't we? Plants and filters. The breathing team.   #warm
cheer: Switching the grow lamps on.
  them: That matters. Light's half of growing.   #funny

== green-hands
when: tier>=friend
them: The garden gave me a habit. I touch every plant I walk past. Just a little. To say hello.
them: On leave, I did it in a shop. To a plastic plant. The shopkeeper stared.   #funny
ask: Has your work given you a habit that follows you around?
listen: Do the plants notice?
  them: I like to think so. The basil grows faster near the path. Make of that what you will.   #warm
share: I water anything that looks thirsty.
  them: Ha. Then you're one of us. Gerald approves.   #funny
cheer: I hum at the lamps when they flicker.
  them: Ha. They like it. Plants and lamps both. Keep humming.   #funny
